  - "The five readings: 1 V \u2192 0.2 A, 2 V \u2192 0.4 A, 3 V \u2192 0.6 A, 4 V
    \u2192 0.8 A, 5 V \u2192 1.0 A."
  - The current increases when the potential difference increases.
  - "Doubling the potential difference doubles the current (1 V \u2192 0.2 A and
    2 V \u2192 0.4 A)."
  doNotSpoil:
  - V is proportional to I as a law statement
  - The straight-line graph (Scene 11)
  - Resistance
